      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is a good and a bad idea at the same time.\n\nGood idea because it allows people to identify whether someone is streaming. Hence, they will know when they're being broadcasted live. That way people can avoid streamers when they do not wish to be in a livestream.\n\nBad idea because said identification draws in the annoying people to only want attention from the streamer, destroying the social atmosphere. Also it makes the streamers a target for crashers, modded client users and harassment which creates a lot of toxicity. Imagine a group of people in a public world sitting in front of a mirror, a streamer comes in and they see the badge that they're livestreaming. Immedietally there's going to be some form of negative response based on a plethora of valid and irrational reasons like not wanting to be in a live stream or having bad experiences with streamers.\n\nPersonally I say no.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
